# REQUIRES: verilator
# The S26 hybrid as a state-home policy (foldsim --state auto --state-home
# hybrid, Driver/Inputs/hybrid): a class's flip-flops and its small RAM (8 x 8
# = 64 bits) stay on chip (their kinds the policy's), its large RAM (64 x 8 =
# 512 bits, at least --hybrid-row-bits) leaves
# the chip as a virtual memory, its rows read from HBM on demand (here the
# testbench's model: latency 1-60 host cycles, stalls, a full controller).
# The simulator matches the target. Mutants: without the hybrid rule the policy
# keeps everything on chip (no virtual memory); at --hybrid-row-bits 1024 the
# large RAM is below the line and stays too.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/hybrid
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/h --static --min-ii 128 --state auto --state-home hybrid --hybrid-row-bits 512 Leaf > %t/h.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=POL < %t/h/state.txt
# POL: frame 128: projected H 128 (II 128, HBM 512 bytes a frame
# POL: virtual memories: ^(Leaf:u_big/mem)$
# POL: storage: {{.*}}Leaf:u_small/mem=block
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH < %t/h/foldsim_sim.vh
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DROWW=6 -Mdir %t/h/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/h/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/h/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/h/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# CHECK-NOT: MISMATCH
# CHECK-NOT: PROTOCOL
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/any --static --min-ii 128 --state auto Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ANY < %t/any/state.txt
# ANY: virtual memories: none
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/hi --static --min-ii 128 --state auto --state-home hybrid --hybrid-row-bits 1024 Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ANY < %t/hi/state.txt
# --hbm-calibration (the card's measured asl9 HBM, every SLR busy): the
# policy's rate is the SLRs' read rates summed (42.9 GB/s = 214.6 B a host
# cycle at 200 MHz, not the assumed 640) and its round trip the loaded one
# (2,401 ns = 481 host cycles): the large RAM's reads wait in bubbles.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/cal --static --min-ii 128 --state auto --state-home hybrid --hybrid-row-bits 512 --hbm-calibration %foldsim_tools/calibrations/hbm-asl9-20261114.json Leaf > /dev/null 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CAL < %t/cal/state.txt
# CAL: frame 128: projected H {{[0-9]+}} (II 128, HBM 512 bytes a frame = 3 host cycles at 214.6 B, bubbles at most {{[1-9][0-9]+}})
